From 4acfb6453971abc4826e2d7e73c1cfc9d0aa24c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:55:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 02/39] Speed up operator setup and nf2ff, add engine export
 hooks (snapshot cg9)

Operator setup: CalcTimestep_Var3 and the Calc_ECOperatorPos loop run on
GetNumSetupThreads() threads with direct index arithmetic; vPrims passed by
const& through Calc_ECPos/Calc_EffMatPos/AverageMat*/GetMaterial; GetMaterial
caches the last lookup per thread; GetDiscDelta tabulated in Init_EC; the
excitation extension skips lines without excitation primitives.
OPENEMS_SETUP_TIMING=1 prints the phase times. Patch x5 4.1 -> 0.9 s,
notch x3 4.1 -> 1.3 s. Bit-identical to stock on all bench models and the
cylindrical multigrid example.

nf2ff: on Cartesian planes the phase factor separates per mesh line, so
N/L are one cgemm (Accelerate, APPLE only) per plane plus a row dot.
Legacy loop kept for cylindrical meshes and OPENEMS_NF2FF_LEGACY=1.
3-D 91x181 pattern x2 freq: 17.9 -> 1.0 s, within 7e-7 relative.

Export hooks for the Swift/Metal prototype: OPENEMS_EXPORT_OPERATOR=dir
writes the compressed operator and excitation before CreateEngine,
OPENEMS_EXPORT_FIELDS=dir writes the fields after the run.
OPENEMS_FTZ=1 (arm64, opt-in) flushes subnormals in the engine threads.

